      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-02-03_WidnesExaminer_art0022" n="art0022">
        <head>HOCKEY.</head>
        <p>HOCKEY.</p>
        <p>~‘ I! said the player;</p>
        <p>"Because I need a star</p>
        <p>I said</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON TRAINING COLLEGE V. SANKEY LADIES. --An enjoyable game was played at Sankey on Saturday, resulting inn victory for the home team of four goals to nil. The Warrington Ladies played very well during the first half, and would have scored two or three times, had it not been for the splendid way Sankey defended. PENKETH FRIENDS' SCHOOL V. WEASTE.—In favour- able weather a " mixed " team from Weaste visited Penketh and encountered the school team on Saturday. The home team, having won the toss, decided to play with the wind, and, taking advantage of the help thus afforded, proceeded very shortly afterwards to open the scoring. Though the visitors played hard and pluckily throughout the game goals were recorded against them at a steady pace, and at full time the score stood at seven goals to nil. PENKETH FRIENDS' SCHOOL LADIES 2ND XI. v. WARRINGTON SECONDARY SCHOOL 2ND Xl.—Played at Warrington on Saturday. The game was fairly even at first. At half time, Edith Powell had scored twice for Penketh. and Warrington had been successful once. During the second half, the home team played an excel- lent defensive game, the backs meeting the Penketh forwards boldly though without being able to prevent them scoring three times. Towards the end Warring- ton gained another goal making the result :—Penketh, five; Warrington, two.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-02-03_WidnesExaminer_art0023" n="art0023">
