      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-02-03_WidnesExaminer_art0074" n="art0074">
        <head>Warrington P.S.A. Society.</head>
        <p>Warrington P.S.A. Society.</p>
        <p>What Other Pea</p>
        <p>t</p>
        <p>The first of a series of three special open meetings in connection with the Warrington P.S.A. Society was held in the Co-operative Hall, Sankey-street,on Sunday and was well attended. Mr. Joseph Owen presided, and Councillor Evans gave the address. He pointed out many advantages the young men of to-day had over the young men of 50 yea' ago, and urged each one present to make the best possible use of the improved conditions of life. Miss Leicester rendered two solos in an able manner, Mr. B. Wadsworth acted as accompanist. Mr. R. Nelson also took part in the meeting.</p>
        <p>Arrangements for dealing with the 200 families which Lord Rothschild has offered to emigrate to Canada have beenrcompleted, and the first batch of about 50 families will sail from Liverpool tn February 13 by the steamer Lake Manitoba.</p>
        <p>The President of the Equitable Life Assurance Society of the United states has announced that the Society has ceased to accept now business from Australia, Russia, Norway, and Sweden, as its policy is to withdraw from the unprofitable quarters of tht world. Irishmen in the United States have cabled .1:1,000 for the funds of the Nationalist patty.</p>
